                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9c32ed7-534a-3591-aa30-65efe430eb26",
                        "entry_id": "6f430967-30fc-3783-8aa9-25c52dc05fdd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière transitoire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81d45b10-4f45-4537-89de-c859ad6a7558",
                                "sense_id": "a9c32ed7-534a-3591-aa30-65efe430eb26",
                                "text": "Ayant travaillé à travers tout le nord et jusqu’à la ville morte de chercheurs d’or de Hall’s Creek, là-bas au sud des Kymberley, […], elles avaient finalement jété l’ancre au bord de l’Ord. Transitoirement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "782e17e8-aefa-4ea4-bfea-719432019b86",
                                "sense_id": "a9c32ed7-534a-3591-aa30-65efe430eb26",
                                "text": "Celui qui étaye va devenir transitoirement la matrice psychique, le décrypteur de sens de celui qui blessé, ne pense plus. C’est dans la relation avec l’autre que la personne psychotraumatisée va pouvoir se remettre à penser."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75514719-e137-4b0c-bc49-13f3d8a8cd83",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f430967-30fc-3783-8aa9-25c52dc05fdd",
                        "source_sense_id": "a9c32ed7-534a-3591-aa30-65efe430eb26",
                        "target_lang_word": "transitorily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transitorily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "793335fd-f942-382c-b7da-133b07227849",
                                        "entry_id": "49e8c15e-0961-3c6a-98e0-cb3563bf4234",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a transitory way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54b354e4-0bde-461f-ac89-4e2dadb09a81",
                                                "sense_id": "793335fd-f942-382c-b7da-133b07227849",
                                                "text": "It is not a permanent space: it transitorily colonizes public urban space, overlapping and somehow replacing it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb00932b-2493-4ae3-8a2a-3548cfc71cc0",
                                                "sense_id": "793335fd-f942-382c-b7da-133b07227849",
                                                "text": "Most transitorily poor households are substantially better off than chronically poor households."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71758b18-93f1-4d94-a7da-05511c444066",
                                                "sense_id": "793335fd-f942-382c-b7da-133b07227849",
                                                "text": "With regard to similes of this kind, it will readily occur to the reader that when a resembling subject is once properly introduced in a simile, the mind is transitorily amused with the new object, and is not dissatisfied with the slight interruption."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ed4343e-8ac8-42a0-80cd-0e44307c2f78",
                                                "sense_id": "793335fd-f942-382c-b7da-133b07227849",
                                                "text": "All parts of the experienced world are experienced transitorily. They appear and disappear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
